# Copy to .env and fill in. Or don't: `python3 scripts/setup_local.py` writes
# this file for you, deriving the database settings from a Commerce_Integration
# .env when it can find one.
#
# NOTHING HERE IS NEEDED to run the planning pages locally. The seeded data in
# data/dev_seed covers every required file, so a clone with no .env at all still
# serves. These variables buy live figures and the weekly run, not a working
# service.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Databases. Both are the same two the Commerce app reads, described
# differently: it holds one connection URL each, this repo holds five discrete
# variables each.
#
# Read the names carefully, because they run backwards from what you would
# guess. COMMERCE_DB_* is the SUPABASE LOOKUP database, not the Commerce app's
# primary one. Wiring these two the wrong way round is the easy mistake, and it
# fails as missing tables rather than as a connection error.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Primary, shipcore schema. Commerce calls this DATABASE_URL.
# Read for: containers and container items (confirmed and draft inbound),
# sc_products names, fc_stats.
DB_HOST=
DB_PORT=5432
DB_NAME=
DB_USER=
DB_PASSWORD=

# Supabase lookup, ecommerce_data schema. Commerce calls this
# SUPABASE_LOOKUP_DATABASE_URL.
# Read for: on-hand, allocated, available and backorder per warehouse.
COMMERCE_DB_HOST=
COMMERCE_DB_PORT=5432
COMMERCE_DB_NAME=
COMMERCE_DB_USER=
COMMERCE_DB_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared with the Commerce app. Copy the values, do not invent them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Sent by Next.js as the x-forecast-token header. Must be byte-identical to the
# Commerce app's variable of the same name, or every endpoint except /health
# returns 401 and the planning pages report the service as unreachable.
FORECAST_API_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The weekly forecast run only. Not needed for local development.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Step 0a of run_forward_forecast.py posts to the Commerce app's velocity sync
# endpoint before forecasting. Both must be set or the step is skipped with a
# message, which is fine locally and not fine on the cron machine.
VELOCITY_SYNC_URL=
VELOCITY_SYNC_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pushing data to the server, and checking it afterwards. Read by
# scripts/push_data_to_server.sh and scripts/verify_deployment.sh, which are how
# each weekly forecast reaches the deployed service: the deploy carries code
# only, and excludes data/ precisely so it cannot overwrite these files.
#
# Needed only on the machine that runs the Monday cron. Nothing here affects
# local development.
#
# Distinct from the GitHub Actions secrets that deploy the code, which are named
# DEPLOY_* and live in the repository settings rather than in this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
FORECAST_DEPLOY_HOST=
FORECAST_DEPLOY_USER=
FORECAST_DEPLOY_PATH=/opt/coverland-forecast-api
FORECAST_DEPLOY_PORT=22

# A PATH to a private key, not the key itself: it becomes `ssh -i <path>`. Leave
# it empty to let ssh resolve a key the usual way. The key it names has to be
# authorised on the server, so taking over the cron means having your own key
# added there rather than inheriting someone else's file.
#
# A tilde is expanded by the deploy scripts, which the shell will not do for a
# value read from this file.
FORECAST_DEPLOY_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REMOVED 2026-08-13. LLM_BASE_URL, LLM_API_KEY, LLM_MODEL and FORECAST_SELF_URL
# configured the /chat assistant on the Demand Forecast page. That endpoint and
# src/chat.py were deleted: chat.py addressed port 8001, where nothing has ever
# listened, so its tool calls failed silently for the whole life of the
# deployment and nobody used it. Setting these now does nothing. Listed here
# rather than deleted outright so that anyone copying an older .env knows why
# their values stopped appearing in this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
